  "temporary_surface_rule":"TEMP_SANDBOX assets are internal working material only. Their descriptors may not admit OUTPUT, MIGRATE or ARCHIVE and may not use AUTHORITY, DELIVERY, DELIVERY_HISTORY, MIGRATED_HISTORY or ARCHIVE roles. CREATE/UPDATE/READ/DELETE may support temporary work; user delivery or durable promotion must target a separate admitted persistent asset or the temp asset must be discarded.",
  "local_workspace_rule":"Durable local filesystem/workspace records use LOCAL_WORKSPACE. CREATE is atomic no-replace. UPDATE uses no-follow dirfd traversal and, when expected_current_hash is supplied, holds an advisory exclusive lock on the bound parent directory across hash verification and atomic rename and rechecks content immediately before commit. This serializes cooperating UAOS local-workspace writers but does not claim linearizability against external writers that ignore the lock. Any exception after the link/rename commit point is UNKNOWN until reconciled rather than FAILED.",
